{
  "esm": "0.6.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "duo_primal_topology",
    "description": "DUO primal unstructured connectivity as a declarative value-invention FAQ (RFC semiring-faq-unified-ir §7.3 / §5.5; bead esd-heg.1 / D1a). Replaces the imperative per-binding edge/connectivity construction (src/grids/duo.jl `_build_connectivity` + `_vertex_faces` and the Rust/Python/TS equivalents) with the landed M3 relational engine. Two index sets are VALUE-INVENTED here, the two remaining arrays are DERIVED from them by relational primitives: (1) `edge_set` is the index-set-producing aggregate (semiring bool_and_or, distinct:true) that ENUMERATES the unique undirected edges from the face->vertex relation of the triangular icosahedral mesh — it iterates each face `f` and its three local edges `le` (slot `le` is the edge OPPOSITE local vertex `le`: le=1->(v2,v3), le=2->(v3,v1), le=3->(v1,v2)), mints a canonical Skolem key skolem(edge, edge_endpoint_a[f,le], edge_endpoint_b[f,le]) per local edge (skolem canonicalizes to the sorted (min,max) vertex pair), and the `true` body marks existence; `distinct` dedups to the content-addressed edge set in the §5.5 sorted order (NOT the binding-divergent Dict-insertion order the imperative builders emitted), exposed as the kind:\"derived\" index set `edges` via from_faq:\"edge_set\". (2) `rank` over `edges` assigns dense ids for the array backend (Julia emits 1-based; the conformance golden normalizes to canonical 0-based). (3) `vertex_face_set` is the second value-invention aggregate: `distinct` over the (vertex, face) incidence of the same connectivity yields the GROUP-BY basis — the sorted (vertex, face) relation, exposed as the derived set `vertex_face_incidence`; the ragged `vertex_faces[v]` (faces-incident-to-vertex) is its per-vertex partition (contiguous + ascending because the sort key is (vertex, face)). The two remaining arrays are relational DERIVATIONS of the enumerated edge set — each materialized by the corresponding `EarthSciSerialization.Relational` primitive in the evaluation bridge (src/topology_faq.jl), not the numeric AST, because join.on keys on index equality rather than on a Skolem expression: `edges_on_face[f,le]` is the dense edge id of each triangle's three edges — the face->edge gather against the `rank` numbering (edge_dense_id of skolem(edge_endpoint_a[f,le], edge_endpoint_b[f,le])); `cell_neighbors[f,le]` is the cell across local edge `le` of face `f` — the connectivity-INVERSION `equijoin` of the (dense edge id, cell, slot) incidence on the shared edge id, keeping the opposite cell (0 = boundary; a closed icosahedral mesh has none). Because the connectivity is build-time-constant (CONST cadence), the entire topology folds into the setup artifact off the per-step hot path (cadence-partition §6.1), exactly as the `pure_topology` fixture: this is a value-invention document, not a dynamical model. Cross-binding byte-identity is guaranteed by the ESS determinism contract (CONFORMANCE_SPEC.md §5.5) and pinned for icos_level0/1/2 in tests/conformance/grids/duo/topology/.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciDiscretizations/polecats/gastown.furiosa"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "duo",
      "icosahedral",
      "primal-topology",
      "unstructured",
      "aggregate",
      "skolem",
      "distinct",
      "rank",
      "equijoin",
      "group-by",
      "value-invention",
      "cadence-partition",
      "declarativization",
      "esd-heg.1"
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "DuoPrimalTopology": {
      "index_sets": {
        "faces": { "kind": "interval", "size": 20 },
        "vertices": { "kind": "interval", "size": 12 },
        "local_edges": { "kind": "interval", "size": 3 },
        "local_verts": { "kind": "interval", "size": 3 },
        "edges": { "kind": "derived", "from_faq": "edge_set" },
        "vertex_face_incidence": { "kind": "derived", "from_faq": "vertex_face_set" }
      },
      "variables": {
        "edge_endpoint_a": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": ["faces", "local_edges"],
          "description": "First endpoint vertex id of each face-local edge (mesh connectivity, CONST). Local edge `le` of triangle (v1,v2,v3) is the edge opposite local vertex `le`: le=1->(v2,v3), le=2->(v3,v1), le=3->(v1,v2). `skolem` canonicalizes (a,b) to the sorted pair, so the raw orientation here is immaterial."
        },
        "edge_endpoint_b": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": ["faces", "local_edges"],
          "description": "Second endpoint vertex id of each face-local edge (mesh connectivity, CONST). Paired with edge_endpoint_a per (face, local_edge)."
        },
        "face_vertex": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": ["faces", "local_verts"],
          "description": "The three vertex ids of each triangular face (mesh connectivity, CONST) — the face->vertex relation that `vertex_face_set` inverts into the group-by basis."
        },
        "edge_exists": {
          "type": "state",
          "shape": ["edges"],
          "description": "Materialized edge-membership over the derived `edges` set, assigned algebraically (not D/dt) from the CONST connectivity — the index-set-producing aggregate output. Declared `state` for a balanced system; the cadence partition's observed-variable elimination folds it out of the (empty) hot path."
        },
        "edge_dense_id": {
          "type": "state",
          "shape": ["edges"],
          "description": "Dense integer ids over the derived `edges` set (the array-backend index), assigned from the `rank` of the sorted distinct edge set. `edges_on_face[f,le]` reads this numbering (the face->edge gather: edge_dense_id of skolem(edge_endpoint_a[f,le], edge_endpoint_b[f,le])), and `cell_neighbors` is the equijoin inversion of the (edge_dense_id, face, le) incidence — both materialized by the relational engine in src/topology_faq.jl."
        },
        "vertex_face_exists": {
          "type": "state",
          "shape": ["vertex_face_incidence"],
          "description": "Materialized membership over the derived `vertex_face_incidence` set — the value-invented (vertex, face) group-by basis. Declared `state` for balance; CONST-folded out of the hot path by the partition."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "_comment": "(1)+(2) edge_set -> `edges`: the index-set-producing node referenced by index_sets.edges.from_faq. semiring bool_and_or + distinct:true dedups the unique undirected edges discovered from the face->vertex connectivity; ranges iterate each face `f` and its three local edges `le`; `key` mints the canonical Skolem term skolem(edge, edge_endpoint_a[f,le], edge_endpoint_b[f,le]) (skolem sorts the endpoints to (min,max)); the `true` body marks existence. Output order is the §5.5 sorted order — the cross-binding byte-stable edge numbering that replaces the imperative builders' Dict-insertion order. This is the literal RFC §7.3 mesh-edge-enumeration form (the relational operation einsum cannot do).",
          "lhs": {
            "op": "index",
            "args": ["edge_exists", "e"]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "id": "edge_set",
            "args": ["edge_endpoint_a", "edge_endpoint_b"],
            "semiring": "bool_and_or",
            "distinct": true,
            "output_idx": ["e"],
            "ranges": {
              "f": { "from": "faces" },
              "le": { "from": "local_edges" }
            },
            "key": {
              "op": "skolem",
              "args": [
                "edge",
                { "op": "index", "args": ["edge_endpoint_a", "f", "le"] },
                { "op": "index", "args": ["edge_endpoint_b", "f", "le"] }
              ]
            },
            "filter": { "op": "true", "args": [] },
            "expr": { "op": "true", "args": [] }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "(2) rank -> `edge_dense_id`: dense integer ids over the derived `edges` set, by position in the sorted distinct sequence (§5.5). All-CONST, folds at compile.",
          "lhs": {
            "op": "index",
            "args": ["edge_dense_id", "e"]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "args": [],
            "semiring": "sum_product",
            "output_idx": ["e"],
            "ranges": { "e": { "from": "edges" } },
            "expr": { "op": "rank", "args": ["edges"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "(3) vertex_face_set -> `vertex_face_incidence`: the SECOND value-invention. distinct over the (vertex, face) incidence of the connectivity — for each face `f` and its three local vertices `lv`, the directed Skolem key skolem(vertex_face, face_vertex[f,lv], f) names the (vertex, face) pair; `distinct` sorts by (vertex, face) and dedups, so the result is the face->vertex GROUP-BY basis. The ragged `vertex_faces[v]` (sorted faces incident on vertex v) is this set's per-vertex partition.",
          "lhs": {
            "op": "index",
            "args": ["vertex_face_exists", "vf"]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "id": "vertex_face_set",
            "args": ["face_vertex"],
            "semiring": "bool_and_or",
            "distinct": true,
            "output_idx": ["vf"],
            "ranges": {
              "f": { "from": "faces" },
              "lv": { "from": "local_verts" }
            },
            "key": {
              "op": "skolem",
              "args": [
                "vertex_face",
                { "op": "index", "args": ["face_vertex", "f", "lv"] },
                "f"
              ]
            },
            "filter": { "op": "true", "args": [] },
            "expr": { "op": "true", "args": [] }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
